# Design System

UI in `apps/web` must use the shared theme and components.

---

## Theme

Theme tokens live in [apps/web/src/index.css](apps/web/src/index.css) (`@theme` block).

Use Tailwind utilities that reference these tokens instead of raw palette classes:

- **Backgrounds**: `bg-bg-base`, `bg-bg-surface`, `bg-bg-elevated`
- **Actions**: `bg-primary` / `text-primary-contrast`, `bg-secondary` / `text-secondary-contrast`
- **Text**: `text-text`, `text-text-muted`
- **Borders**: `border-border`
- **Semantic**: `text-error`, `text-success`, `bg-error`, etc.

Do not use raw neutrals (e.g. `neutral-900`, `neutral-500`) or other palette colours (e.g. `sky-500`, `red-500`) when a theme token exists for the intent.

---

## Components

Reusable components live in [apps/web/src/components](apps/web/src/components).

- **Buttons**: Use the `Button` component with `variant` (primary, secondary, ghost, danger) and `size` (sm, md, lg). Use `asChild` with `Link` for navigation that should look like a button.
- **Modals**: Use the `Modal` component (title, body, optional footer, `onClose`).
- **Forms**: Use `Input` (with optional `label`, `error`) and `Label` for form fields.
- **Panels**: Use `Card` for bordered content blocks (optional `title`).

Do not add one-off styled `<button>`, `<input>`, or modal markup when the design system provides an equivalent component.

---

## Adding to the design system

New tokens go in `index.css` (`@theme`). New primitives go in `apps/web/src/components`. Keep variants and props minimal; extend when needed.
